cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ActionsBench, please cite it as below and state the corpus version you used."
title: "ActionsBench: a labeled benchmark for GitHub Actions workflow security scanners"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tijani
    given-names: Aliu
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
repository-code: "https://github.com/NeesimEra/ActionsBench"
url: "https://github.com/NeesimEra/ActionsBench"
abstract: >-
  A labeled corpus of minimized GitHub Actions workflows, each tagged with the weakness it contains or marked
  clean, and a harness that scores workflow security scanners against it per weakness class. The code is MIT
  licensed and the corpus is CC BY 4.0. Version 0.1.0 is an initial release (pre-1.0): 44 hand-built cases, all labels
  proposed by one author and audited against primary sources but not independently reviewed.
keywords:
  - github-actions
  - security
  - benchmark
  - static-analysis
